      "n_contexts": 12,
      "answer": "The context does not describe a regulatory path from the FAA to the maintenance crew for the CFM LEAP-1B engine. It separately states that FAA airworthiness directives are legally enforceable rules applying to aircraft, aircraft engines, propellers, and appliances (\u00a7 39.3), and that the 737 MAX CMM lists applicable ADs for LEAP-1B engine mount inspection (FAA AD 2024-01-02, FAA AD 2022-03-07, CFM AD CFM-2023-14), but it does not state a chain or process linking FAA issuance to maintenance-crew action for that engine.",
