      "n_contexts": 12,
      "answer": "The 2022 directive (FAA AD 2022-03-07) supersedes AD 2020-05-11, and is itself superseded by AD 2024-01-02. AD 2024-01-02's references state that AD 2020-05-11 was \"partially superseded by AD 2022-03-07, fully superseded by this AD.\"\n\nFor current operators, this means AD 2024-01-02 is the operative directive: it requires MCAS Software v2.0 (or later) installation within 90 days of its February 15, 2024 effective date, and the MCAS Software v2.0 release notes state that 737-8/737-9 aircraft must not be operated with MCAS v1.7.3 or earlier after the AD's compliance date. The context does not state any further relationship beyond these supersession facts.",
