      "n_contexts": 12,
      "answer": "No. The January 2024 inspection report and the March 2024 AD compliance report do not contradict each other on the aircraft's compliance status.\n\n- The inspection report (completed January 19, 2024) records G-ABCD as compliant with FAA AD 2022-03-07 (MCAS v1.7.3 installed, AOA Disagree Alert active) and FAA AD 2020-05-11, and states the aircraft is airworthy.\n- The March 2024 compliance report likewise lists AD 2022-03-07 and AD 2020-05-11 as compliant, and flags AD 2024-01-02 (MCAS v2.0) as non-compliant only because the May 15, 2024 deadline had not yet been reached, noting the aircraft remains airworthy under MCAS v1.7.3 until that deadline.\n\nThe reports are consistent: both show compliance with the earlier ADs and identify the MCAS v2.0 requirement as an upcoming (not yet due) action.",
