      "answer": "14 CFR Part 39 establishes requirements for correcting unsafe conditions in aircraft, aircraft engines, propellers, and appliances when those conditions exist or are likely to exist or develop in other products of the same design. It also defines airworthiness directives as legally enforceable rules applying to those products.\n\nThe FAA airworthiness directives in the context are issued under 14 CFR Part 39 (e.g., FAA AD 2020-05-11, 2022-03-07, and 2024-01-02 each cite 14 CFR Part 39). The context does not identify a single directive as \"the\" one referencing Part 39.",
